%% UC-44 — Enrol with a verified code (+ UC-45, the study consent that follows)
%%
%% The whole point of the reserve/confirm/release shape is that this flow spans
%% TWO databases with no shared transaction: the register's PostgreSQL and
%% HHH's Mongo/Neo4j. A single-phase redeem would mark the code used and then
%% lose the Neo4j write, burning the code and forcing a nurse to issue a
%% replacement. Reserving first leaves a state that is recoverable from either
%% side.
%%
%% Note what does NOT cross the boundary: no name, no date of birth, no email.
%% The internal API has no route that returns one.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor P as Participant
    participant F as Flutter App
    participant B as Backend (studyEnrollRouter)
    participant I as identity-service (:3003 internal)
    participant PG as identity-db (PostgreSQL)
    participant M as MongoDB
    participant N as Neo4j

    P->>F: Enter HHV-XXXXX-XXXXX
    Note over F: normalizeStudyCode maps I/L→1 and O→0<br/>ONLY for HHV- codes. Those letters are legal<br/>in anonymous HHH- codes, and mapping them<br/>there would break about a third of them.
    F->>B: POST /api/v1/study/enroll { code }
    B->>B: resolveIdentityConfig(study)<br/>absent ⇒ anonymous

    alt anonymous study (unchanged path)
        B->>M: redeem study code
        B->>N: MERGE (:User)-[:ENROLLED_IN]->(:Study)
        B-->>F: 200 { studyId, groupId }
    else verified study
        B->>I: POST /internal/v1/codes/reserve { code }<br/>x-service-auth-token
        I->>PG: lookup by HMAC digest, mark reserved
        PG-->>I: subjectCode, reservationId, expiresAt
        I-->>B: { reservationId, hhhStudyId, subjectCode, expiresAt }
        Note over I,B: Returns a CODE and nothing else.<br/>No name has crossed this edge.

        B->>N: MERGE (:User)-[:ENROLLED_IN]->(:Study)
        alt Neo4j write succeeded
            B->>M: upsert enrollment { subjectCode, studyCodeUsed: null }
            B->>I: POST /internal/v1/codes/confirm { reservationId, keycloakSub, hhhGroupId }
            I->>PG: encrypt sub, insert link, mark code redeemed
            Note over PG: partial unique index on<br/>superseded_at IS NULL ⇒ one live link.<br/>A replacement code supersedes the old one<br/>rather than creating a second subject.
            B-->>F: 200 { studyId, groupId, subjectCode }
        else Neo4j or Mongo write failed
            B->>I: POST /internal/v1/codes/release { reservationId }
            I->>PG: back to 'issued'
            B-->>F: 500 — the code is still usable
            Note over I,PG: If the backend dies before releasing,<br/>the sweeper reclaims it within<br/>IDENTITY_RESERVATION_TTL_MINUTES (default 10).
        end
    end

    %% ---- UC-45: the study consent that can only happen now ----
    F->>B: GET /api/v1/onboarding/enrollment
    B-->>F: { studyConsentPending: true, documentSlug }
    Note over F: The study — and therefore which consent<br/>document to show — is unknown until the code<br/>is redeemed. That is why this is a router gate<br/>after enrolment, not a sixth onboarding screen.
    F->>B: GET /api/v1/consent?slug=<slug>&lang=<lang>
    B->>M: study_consent_documents (slug, lang)
    alt a row exists
        M-->>B: edited in the admin portal
    else no row
        B->>B: fall back to app/language/<lang>/consent-<slug>.md
    end
    B-->>F: rendered HTML + { version, effectiveDate }
    P->>F: Accept
    F->>B: POST /api/v1/consent { version, documentSlug, locale }
    B->>M: append to consents
    Note over B,M: documentSlug distinguishes this from the platform<br/>consent: consentVersion is a bare semver, so a study's<br/>1.0.0 would otherwise satisfy a check for the platform's.
